# Tangent–symmedian lemma — the tangents to the circumcircle at B and C meet on the A-symmedian: AT is the reflection of the median in the bisector (source: Evan Chen, EGMO Lemma 4.26)
A B C = triangle
O = circumcenter(A, B, C)
T = meet(perp_line(B, line(O, B)), perp_line(C, line(O, C)))
Ma = midpoint(B, C)
prove eqangle(A, B, A, T, A, Ma, A, C)
